  "recipeCuisine": "Malaysia",
  "name": "Chinese Fish Ball Soup - Bee Hoon",
  "text": "Chinese Fish Ball Soup - Bee Hoon\n\nYield: 4-6\n\nPreparation time: 20 minutes\n\nCooking time: 10 minutes\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the fish balls\n\n450g white fish fillets (haddock, cod, bream - boned and flaked),\n\n1 - 2 tbsp rice flour,\n\nSalt and ground black pepper.\n\nFor the soup\n\n1 ½ l fish or chicken stock,\n\n1 - 2 tbsp light soy sauce,\n\n4-6 mustard green leaves (chopped),\n\n90 g mung bean thread noodles (soaked in hot water until soft).\n\nFor the garnish\n\n2 spring onions,\n\n1 red or green chilli,\n\nFresh coriander leaves (chopped).\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Bring the stock to the boil.\n\n2. Meanwhile make the fish balls.\n\n2.1 Grind the flaked fish into a paste using a mortar and pestle or a food processor.\n\n2.2 Season with salt and pepper.\n\n2.3 Stir in 4 tbsp water.\n\n2.4 Sprinkle with rice flour and mould into balls.\n\n3. Season stock and add fish balls, simmering for 5 minutes.\n\n4. Add the shredded mustard greens and simmer for 1 minute.\n\n5. Divide the noodles between the bowls.\n\n6. Put the fish balls and soup into the bowls.\n\n7. Garnish with spring onions, chilli, and chopped coriander.",
  "recipeYield": "4-6",
